# boost.version has no module-import edges.
#
# SPECIAL tier (C5, plan .agents/plan/2026-09-09-boost-version-module-promotion.md):
# the entire module TU consists of two `inline constexpr` constants seeded
# from <boost/version.hpp> via `module; #include` in src/version.cppm. The
# constants have no signatures referring to other boost::* entities (the
# BOOST_VERSION int is 109100 and BOOST_LIB_VERSION is "1_91" — both
# literals), so the dep_graph BFS over signatures and the pass-2 body walk
# both produce the empty edge set. There is no gen_exports.py bundle TU
# for this library at all (it's bypassed in the SPECIAL tier, like log/test
# are bypassed via LIBS_COMPILED_INCLUDE_ONLY but mirrored — SPECIAL has a
# .cppm, log/test don't).
#
# This file exists to satisfy the "every target lib has a .deps sibling"
# convention so maintainers don't wonder why version.cppm has no
# corresponding export list. gen_features.py's deps_of() returns the empty
# set when the file is missing, so functionally this file is optional; it
# is documentation, not data.
